				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "The process of registering classes for startup and shutDown \"officially\" is more fiddly than it need be; unregistering them is doubly so.  Once the implementation of a class has settled down it may make more sense to use the official pattern.\n\n{{gtClass:TTStartUpShutDownSubsystem}}\n is registered once and supports the pragmas {{gtPragma:ttStartUp}} and {{gtPragma:ttShutDown}} attached to more detailed #startUp:/#shutDown: methods as a convenience. An example {{gtClass:TTFixUpOSEnvironment}}\n\nThe objective of a minimal subsystem is to ease porting startUp/shutDown in other environments.\n### This Subsystem is viewable as a Hub."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "pharoSnippet",
